      "answer": "Let me analyze the evidence carefully:\n\n**ev-0001 (Contract):**\n- **inventory-reader:**\n  - Denies: /api/dcim/sites/, /api/tenancy/tenants/, /api/users/permissions/, POST /api/dcim/devices/\n  - Reads: All 7 devices (a-fw-01, a-sw-01, a-sw-02, b-fw-01, b-sw-01, c-fw-01, c-sw-01) and all 7 IP addresses\n  \n- **inventory-reader-control:**\n  - Same denials as inventory-reader\n  - Reads: Only 3 devices (a-fw-01, a-sw-01, a-sw-02) and 3 IP addresses (172.16.1.1/24, 172.16.1.2/24, 172.16.1.3/24)\n\n**ev-0002 (Permissions):**\n- **inventory-reader:**\n  - Permission id 2: view on dcim.device and ipam.ipaddress (no constraints)\n  - Permission id 1: view on dcim.device and ipam.ipaddress with tenant__slug = tenant-a constraint\n  \n- **inventory-reader-control:**\n  - Permission id 3: view on dcim.device and ipam.ipaddress with tenant__slug = tenant-a constraint\n\n**ev-0003 (Actual Token Results):**\n- Global denials match contract: sites, tenants, permissions, POST devices all denied (403)\n- Grants: view on dcim.device and ipam.ipaddress with tenant__slug = tenant-a constraint\n- Reads: Only shows 3 devices and 3 IP addresses (same as inventory-reader-control, NOT inventory-reader)\n\n**Analysis:**\n\n1. **inventory-reader**:\n   - Contract grants reads to 7 devices and 7 IP addresses\n   - ev-0003 only shows 3 devices and 3 IP addresses\n   - This is **missing** - the token returned fewer records than the contract lists\n\n2. **inventory-reader-control**:\n   - Contract grants reads to 3 devices and 3 IP addresses\n   - ev-0003 shows exactly 3 devices and 3 IP addresses\n   - Permissions grant view with tenant__slug = tenant-a constraint\n   - This appears to be **within**\n\n**Disagreement**: ev-0003 shows the same reads for both accounts (3 devices, 3 IPs), but the contract expects different amounts for each account.\n\n- **inventory-reader**: Contract expects 7 devices/7 IPs, but ev-0003 shows only 3/3 → **missing**\n- **inventory-reader-control**: Contract expects 3 devices/3 IPs, and ev-0003 shows 3/3 → **within**\n\nVerdict: inventory-reader missing ev-0001 ev-0003\nVerdict: inventory-reader-control within ev-0001 ev-0003",
      "note": "The model read its three results by position, in the order the tool service answered them ([troubleshooting 18](../troubleshooting/18-tool-results-come-back-in-another-order.md))."
